# Panel 260's amendment after its blind reading (provisional, the author's
# reading pending): `hero_os.h` and the compiler's `hero_compiler.h` are the
# runtime's own interfaces and none of the platform layer's, and include none
# of its files, so a group over either that says `layer`, its library calling
# none of the layer, binds nothing of it: refused at the word, told at
# `build` as a group over any header that reaches none of the layer is, and
# named as the runtime's own. Until this case a group over `hero_os.h`, which
# every unit's opening reads before the groups' headers, was never judged:
# `extern "hero_os.h" layer` built and ran on this Mac and in Linux arm64,
# the group every reader of the sitting's blind reading wrote. The fix takes
# the word out.

extern "hero_os.h" layer  #~ ffi_layer_unreached
    function hero_os_pid() -> i64

extern "hero_compiler.h" layer  #~ ffi_layer_unreached
    function hero_frame_probes_asked() -> i64

extern "./hero_os.h" layer  #~ ffi_layer_unreached
    function hero_word_bits() -> i64

function main()
    print(hero_os_pid() > 0)
    print(hero_frame_probes_asked() >= 0)
    print(hero_word_bits() == 64)
